This product is an Apple MLX hand-port of ByteDance Lance, a 3B unified
multimodal model.  It is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(see LICENSE).

================================================================================
Upstream works (all Apache-2.0) this port is derived from / depends on
================================================================================

1. ByteDance Lance — original PyTorch model, architecture, and weights.
   https://huggingface.co/bytedance-research/Lance
   https://github.com/bytedance/Lance
   Licensed under Apache-2.0.

   The MLX weights published alongside this repo
   (avlp12/Lance-3B-Alis-MLX-Traced) are an F32, deterministic conversion of
   the original Lance image + video weights.  The image weight is bit-identical
   (same SHA256) with RockTalk/Lance-3B-MLX (F32), which converts the same
   source; a separate bf16 build is mlx-community/Lance-3B-bf16.

2. Alibaba Wan 2.2 — 3D Causal VAE architecture (the video VAE ported in
   STAGE 5/8).
   https://github.com/Wan-Video/Wan2.2
   Licensed under Apache-2.0.

3. Qwen2.5-VL-3B-Instruct (Alibaba Qwen team) — vision-language backbone and
   tokenizer that Lance builds on.
   https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2.5-VL-3B-Instruct
   Licensed under Apache-2.0.

4. RockTalk — independent MLX checkpoint conversion + standalone weight
   layout, used in this repo as a byte-diff parity reference (STAGE 1).
   https://huggingface.co/RockTalk/Lance-3B-MLX
   https://huggingface.co/RockTalk/Wan2.2-VAE-MLX

================================================================================
Modifications made by this project
================================================================================

- Reimplemented the Lance forward path (Qwen2 backbone + MoT routing, 3D
  mRoPE, Wan 2.2 VAE, ViT adapter, flow-matching + CFG, t2i/t2v/x2t/image_edit
  pipelines) in Apple MLX.  See lance_mlx/.
- Added per-stage byte-diff verification harnesses against the original
  PyTorch (tools/stage*_compare.py) and a per-stage lesson trail
  (LEARNING_LOG/).  Note: two bugs were found and fixed after the initial
  release (ViT patch-token order; x2t_video temporal mRoPE), in the MLX
  pipeline / harness only — the published weights are unchanged.  See the
  repo README "Post-release correction" section.
- Inference runs pure MLX (no torch / refs import at runtime); PyTorch is
  imported only by the verification harnesses.

Apache-2.0 license headers in upstream files under refs/ (fetched separately,
not committed) are preserved verbatim in those files.

